        // ── The galaxy ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        //
        // Space past this system. `galaxy` hashes the void into sectors, rolls
        // a star for the ones that get one, and builds a real system there when
        // the ship comes near — so flying out far enough never runs out of
        // world, and flying back finds the same stars where it left them.
        //
        // It is also the thing that stops the ship outrunning the generator:
        // the warp ladder asks it for a ceiling every frame, and it lowers that
        // ceiling while a system is being built. Generation is what warp is
        // paced against, so the pacing lives with the generator.
        //
        // Appended LAST for the same reason the Pause Menu is: `parent` is a
        // positional index into this list.
        (
            name: "Galaxy",
            transform: (
                translation: (0.0, 0.0, 0.0),
