        // ── The air ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        //
        // Fog, driven from whatever body you are at and how high above it you
        // are. Every world already has a rolled atmosphere that the sky shader
        // draws as a halo from orbit; this is the inside of that same air, so
        // an airless moon looks airless and a thick blue sky reads as one from
        // the ground. In space it switches the pass off entirely.
        //
        // Appended LAST: `parent` is a positional index into this list.
        (
            name: "Atmosphere",
            transform: (
                translation: (0.0, 0.0, 0.0),
